    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0383" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/12261: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-16T18:00:00+01:00"
                            >November 16, 1918—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 17—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2368. Learned that detachment of troops have [occupied?] Fiume, but some doubt
                    exists whether Italians only or international force.</p>
                <p>The Fiume Italian Deputy, who called on me to-day, states that after talk with
                    Premier Orlando, he [sent?] a note to Baron Sonnino the evening the latter left
                    Rome for Paris requesting that Fiume be taken under the Allies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
